# Fourteen putts at hole 1 with the aim and the power varied, which is enough to reach the stroke
# limit and be moved on to the next hole — and enough, on the way, to run half of the hole's state
# machine that no other case reaches: the meter, the ball rolling and stopping, the stroke limit and
# its message, the hole changing underneath the player.
#
# The ball never actually goes in. Sinking it needs an aim this cannot work out from here, so
# `tick_holed` and `tick_sinking` are still the largest thing no case covers.
#
# Checked against the pure recompilation (tests/vs-recomp.sh), not against a recording.
